# Story page: shard
# {name} becomes the snake's name. Paragraphs are separated by a blank line.
title = The Mirror Shard
---
A sliver of the Glass Hall, sharp and bright and careful never to show its good side.

Look into it and something much larger looks back: patient, coiled and horribly familiar, the way a face is familiar when you have only ever seen it reversed.

It winked again. This time, slowly, {name} winked back. I said this was unwise. I said it loudly, and twice. I was ignored, which is the natural condition of narrators.
